---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="KickzBrary Support"
  description="Support information for KickzBrary by HSL Innovations."
>
  <section class="page-hero container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Support</p>
    <div class="page-app-icon">
      <img
        src="/icons/kickzbrary.png"
        alt="KickzBrary app icon"
        class="app-icon"
      />
    </div>
    <h1>KickzBrary</h1>
    <p>
      Need help with KickzBrary? Find collection guidance, troubleshooting tips,
      privacy information, accessibility documentation, and ways to share feedback.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card">
    <h2>Getting Started</h2>
    <p>
      KickzBrary helps you build and enjoy a personal sneaker library. Add the
      pairs you own, keep their important details organized, browse your gallery,
      and view statistics about your collection.
    </p>

    <h2>Managing Your Collection</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Add a sneaker to your library and enter the details you want to keep.</li>
      <li>Add a photo to make the pair easy to recognize in your gallery.</li>
      <li>Edit an existing entry whenever its details need to be updated.</li>
      <li>Delete an entry when you no longer want it in your collection.</li>
      <li>Use the collection views to browse and explore the pairs you have added.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Collection Statistics</h2>
    <p>
      KickzBrary uses the information in your library to provide collection
      statistics. Keeping your sneaker details complete and consistent will help
      the app provide the most useful overview of your collection.
    </p>

    <h2>Import and Export</h2>
    <p>
      Import and export tools help you move or keep a copy of your collection
      data. Review an imported file before confirming changes, and store exported
      files somewhere secure. Exported files are no longer controlled by
      KickzBrary after you save or share them outside the app.
    </p>

    <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        If a photo cannot be added, check that KickzBrary has permission to use
        your photo library or camera in your device settings.
      </li>
      <li>
        If an import does not work, confirm that the file is a supported
        KickzBrary export and has not been modified or damaged.
      </li>
      <li>
        If collection statistics look incomplete, review the details saved for
        your sneaker entries.
      </li>
      <li>
        If the app behaves unexpectedly, close and reopen it, then make sure you
        are using the latest available version.
      </li>
      <li>
        Before reinstalling the app, export any collection information you want
        to keep.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <h3>What information can I save for a sneaker?</h3>
    <p>
      You can save collection details such as the sneaker's name, brand, model,
      size, colorway, purchase information, personal notes, and a photo. The
      available fields may change as KickzBrary evolves.
    </p>

    <h3>Can I edit or remove a sneaker after adding it?</h3>
    <p>
      Yes. You can update an entry when its details change or delete it from your
      collection when you no longer want to keep it.
    </p>

    <h3>Does KickzBrary sell my collection data?</h3>
    <p>
      No. HSL Innovations does not sell your personal information or use your
      collection data to build an advertising profile.
    </p>

    <h3>What should I do before deleting the app?</h3>
    <p>
      Export any collection information you want to keep before deleting the app.
      Removing the app may also remove information stored locally on your device.
    </p>

    <h3>Can I request a new feature?</h3>
    <p>
      Yes. Suggestions for collection fields, organization tools, accessibility
      improvements, and other features are welcome through the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>
      or on Instagram at <a href="https://www.instagram.com/kickzbrary/" rel="noopener noreferrer">@kickzbrary</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy and Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      KickzBrary is designed with privacy and accessibility in mind. You can
      review the related documentation below.
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li><a href="/privacy/kickzbrary">KickzBrary Privacy Policy</a></li>
      <li><a href="/accessibility/kickzbrary">KickzBrary Accessibility Information</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Feedback and Bug Reports</h2>
    <p>
      If you need help, want to report a bug, or have feedback about KickzBrary,
      please contact HSL Innovations through the <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.
      If you are reporting a bug, include your device model, iOS or iPadOS version,
      KickzBrary version, and the steps that led to the issue. Screenshots are
      helpful when available, but please remove any personal information first.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
